  "articleBody": "While some home improvement tasks are perfect for DIY, a basement project often involves complexities that really benefit from professional expertise. So, when should you pick up the phone and call in the pros? If your project involves any kind of waterproofing or moisture remediation, that's a huge sign. Improper waterproofing can lead to big problems down the line. Any significant plumbing, electrical, or HVAC work also falls into this category – these aren't just about functionality, they're about safety and code compliance. Structural changes, even minor ones, should always be handled by experienced professionals. And, of course, if your project requires permits and inspections, a qualified contractor can manage that whole coordination process for you, saving you a lot of potential headaches. At HH Remodeling LLC, we've got the experience to handle these kinds of details, making sure your basement remodel is done right and to code. Don't risk it when it comes to the bones of your home; professional help is an investment in your home's safety and longevity.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}